{
  "name": "vector_light_bake_mask",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "ONE ARM PER RUN: the 'mask' arm of 27's bake cost, recorded as a Circinus run document under the label celestiallighting-mask. Four arms inside one process did not work \u2014 the flag flips stop dirtying the map after the first whole-map rebake, so every arm after the first recorded nothing while the instrumentation stayed live. A process per arm makes 'exactly one rebake' true by construction. The arm's flags are set BEFORE the recorder opens; the measured rebake is a single penumbra toggle off and back on, which returns the arm to the same state so what is timed is a rebake OF this arm rather than a transition between two. circinus_ours_* arms our own postfix rather than vanilla's Regenerate, so the figure is 27's cost and not the 795 ms vanilla already spends baking 112 sections. Compare the run documents in Circinus/Runs/, not readings within one run.",
